From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] generate_abstract: an abstract from global route is timed
 with the route's parasitics

generate_abstract read SPEF for a final-stage abstract and estimated
placement parasitics for every stage from place on, global route
included. An abstract written from 5_1_grt.odb therefore modelled the
block with placement parasitics, while the block itself is timed at
global route with the route's. On a large block the two differ by a
factor: XiangShan's MemBlock times an input-to-output path at 1,840 ps
with global-route parasitics and 6,911 ps with placement parasitics,
and the abstract's liberty carried the 6.9 ns arc into the parent,
where it set the parent's worst paths.

From global route on, without a SPEF, the abstract now estimates
parasitics from the global route, as the stage's own timing does.

Not upstreamed. Retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS that times a
global-route abstract with the route's parasitics.
---
diff --git a/flow/scripts/generate_abstract.tcl b/flow/scripts/generate_abstract.tcl
--- a/flow/scripts/generate_abstract.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/generate_abstract.tcl
@@ -15,6 +15,8 @@
 
 if { $design_stage >= 6 && [file exists $::env(RESULTS_DIR)/$stem.spef] } {
   log_cmd read_spef $::env(RESULTS_DIR)/$stem.spef
+} elseif { $design_stage >= 5 } {
+  log_cmd estimate_parasitics -global_routing
 } elseif { $design_stage >= 3 } {
   log_cmd estimate_parasitics -placement
 }
